Breadslicer
===========

Breadslicer is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License (see
LICENSE.md); each crate states its own license in its Cargo.toml and
LICENSE.md. It includes work from these projects, whose notices are kept in
the source as their licenses require:

- SoulCrafted Slicer (MyMiniFactory Ltd, CTRLback SCCL; AGPL-3.0, with
  libraries under Apache-2.0), which Breadslicer is based on.
  https://codeberg.org/SoulCrafted/Slicer

- DragonFruit (Open Resin Alliance and contributors): the support system,
  ported under AGPL-3.0-or-later, and the hollowing engine, ported from its
  MIT mesh crates. See libs/sc-geom/support-gen-df/NOTICE and
  libs/sc-geom/hollow-df/NOTICE. The bundled Anycubic and ELEGOO printer
  profiles were first converted from its printer plugins, and their product
  images come from them; see assets/profiles/README.md and
  assets/profiles/images/README.md.

- UVtools (Copyright 2020-2026 PTRTECH, Tiago Conceição (sn4k3) and UVtools
  contributors; AGPL-3.0-or-later): the Creality CXDLP printer-file writer,
  the ChiTuBox CTB writer for versions 2 to 4, and the Anycubic ZIP (.pwsz, .pm7, .pm7m, .pm4u, .pp1, .pp1m) and binary
  (.pwmx, .pwma, .pm3, .pws and the rest) printer-file writers, ported to
  Rust from UVtools v7.1.1. See libs/sla-formats-uvtools/NOTICE. The bundled
  printer profiles are converted from the PrusaSlicer printer profiles UVtools
  v7.1.1 bundles (PrusaSlicer/printer/*.ini); see assets/profiles/README.md.
  https://github.com/sn4k3/UVtools

- manifold-rust (Lars Brubaker; Apache-2.0), a Rust port of Manifold (Emmett
  Lalish and contributors; Apache-2.0): its polygon triangulator closes the
  plane cut, and its plane split is the cut's fallback. Used as a crate. See
  libs/cut.
  https://github.com/larsbrubaker/manifold-rust
  https://github.com/elalish/manifold
